---
description: Web app rules (Next.js 15)
globs: apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx},packages/ui/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---
Spec: `docs/prd/03-web.md` (design system §1, screens §4), permissions in `docs/prd/05-rbac-and-nfr.md`.

- App Router. Server Components by default; `"use client"` only where interaction demands it.
- Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui. Use design tokens from §1.1 — never hard-code a hex value.
- Dark mode on every screen from the start, not retrofitted.
- Lists are URL-driven: filters, page, sort live in the query string so views are shareable.
- Data via TanStack Query. Tables via TanStack Table with server-side pagination/sort/filter.
- Forms: react-hook-form + Zod schemas imported from `packages/shared` (same schemas the API validates with).
- Every screen implements loading (skeleton, not spinner), empty (with primary CTA) and error (with traceId) states.
- Permission checks client-side are UX only. Never rely on them for security.
- No `any`. No `useEffect` for data fetching. No inline fetch — use the generated typed API client.
- Accessibility: labels on all inputs, visible focus rings, status never encoded by colour alone.
